Diagram: a running container issues syscalls to the Linux kernel; Falco taps the
syscall stream via an eBPF probe, evaluates each event against rules, and emits an
alert on match — example alert box "Warning: shell spawned in container
(user=root shell=bash container=app)". A timeline shows pre-deploy controls
(scan, policy, sign) ending at deploy, and Falco covering the runtime period
after. Flat style. max-width 860px.
